msgid "Nexus 文档内容与图示标准"
msgstr "Nexus documentation content and diagram standards"

msgid "本标准用于新增和修改的平台文档。目标是让读者明确任务、条件、操作和结果， 能够沿文档完成使用、接入、维护或验收。既有页面按 {download}`实施台账 <documentation-system-execution.csv>`逐批审查；本标准的存在不表示 正文迁移、图册、自动检查、翻译或发布已经完成。"
msgstr "These standards govern new/changed platform documentation so readers understand tasks, conditions, actions and results for use, integration, maintenance or acceptance. Review existing pages in batches using the {download}`implementation ledger <documentation-system-execution.csv>`. These standards do not establish completion of content migration, diagrams, automation, translation or publication."

msgid "必须/不得表示合同要求；应/不应表示默认做法，例外需有理由；可以表示允许的 选择。规范性要求必须明确主体、条件、动作和可检查的结果。责任由 Codex 承担， 独立 agent 进行内容和图示评审，不要求虚构人员账号。"
msgstr "Must/must not express requirements; should/should not express defaults with justified exceptions; may expresses permitted choices. Normative rules must identify actors, conditions, actions and checkable outcomes. Codex owns responsibility; independent agents review content/diagrams without invented human accounts."

msgid "1. 内容必须帮助读者完成任务"
msgstr "1. Content must help readers complete tasks"

msgid "编号"
msgstr "ID"

msgid "约束"
msgstr "Constraint"

msgid "验收方法"
msgstr "Acceptance method"

msgid "TXT-01"
msgstr "TXT-01"

msgid "开头说明读者能完成什么、适用配置和必要限制"
msgstr "Open with outcomes, applicable configuration and essential limitations."

msgid "单看开头能够判断是否适用"
msgstr "Readers can determine applicability from the opening alone."

msgid "TXT-02"
msgstr "TXT-02"

msgid "tutorial/how-to 围绕一个主要目标，先给结果和必要步骤"
msgstr "Tutorials/how-to guides focus on one primary goal, giving outcomes and necessary steps first."

msgid "独立读者能够按步骤完成"
msgstr "Independent readers can complete the steps."

msgid "TXT-03"
msgstr "TXT-03"

msgid "一段围绕一个问题，使用具体主体、主动动词和稳定术语"
msgstr "One paragraph addresses one question with concrete actors, active verbs and consistent terms."

msgid "去掉重复结论、口号和无解释的缩写"
msgstr "Remove repeated conclusions, slogans and unexplained abbreviations."

msgid "TXT-04"
msgstr "TXT-04"

msgid "比较/字段用表；顺序用步骤；结构与并发用对应图"
msgstr "Use tables for comparisons/fields, steps for order, and appropriate diagrams for structure/concurrency."

msgid "表、图、正文各自承担必要信息"
msgstr "Tables, diagrams and prose each carry necessary information."

msgid "TXT-05"
msgstr "TXT-05"

msgid "原始日志、大量hash和失败尝试链接到证据，不打断操作主线"
msgstr "Link raw logs, long hashes and failed attempts as evidence without interrupting main procedures."

msgid "可读摘要能定位完整原件"
msgstr "Readable summaries locate complete originals."

msgid "TXT-06"
msgstr "TXT-06"

msgid "精确区分当前实现、已验证、估计和计划"
msgstr "Separate current implementation, validation, estimates and plans precisely."

msgid "每个能力/性能结论有范围与出处"
msgstr "Every capability/performance claim has scope and provenance."

msgid "TXT-07"
msgstr "TXT-07"

msgid "同一规范只维护一份，概述/翻译/图链接权威合同"
msgstr "Maintain one authoritative standard; summaries/translations/diagrams link it."

msgid "修改接口不需同步两份手写声明"
msgstr "Interface changes do not require two handwritten declarations to be synchronized."

msgid "TXT-08"
msgstr "TXT-08"

msgid "架构和合同改变同时核对受影响图、示例与翻译"
msgstr "Architecture/contract changes review affected diagrams, examples and translations together."

msgid "PR列出影响范围与审查结果"
msgstr "PRs report impacts and review results."

msgid "不设机械字数、句数或图数量门槛。复杂页面需要任务索引和分层说明；简单动作 不强制配图。不能用“极致、完整、全部支持”等无范围结论代替成本和资格记录。"
msgstr "Set no mechanical word, sentence or diagram quotas. Complex pages need task indexes and layered explanations; simple actions need not have diagrams. Unscoped “ultimate”, “complete” or “all supported” claims do not replace cost/qualification records."

msgid "页面采用 [五类内容模板](documentation-templates.md)。模板规定必须回答的问题， 不强制所有页面使用相同标题。当前架构解释需回答：为何分层、谁拥有状态和资源、 谁调用谁、构建与运行各做什么、合法上下文、失败责任、成本及验证边界。"
msgstr "Use the [five page templates](documentation-templates.md). They define required questions without forcing identical headings. Architecture explanations must address why layers exist, state/resource ownership, calls, build/runtime responsibilities, legal context, failure responsibility, cost and validation boundaries."

msgid "2. 术语、单位和约束"
msgstr "2. Terminology, units and constraints"

msgid "首次出现可给中英文对应，随后同一概念使用同一词。C符号、配置键、错误码、 结构字段及CSV/JSON中的机器身份值保持原样，包括状态、ID、摘要、路径、版本和 配置值。原CSV/JSON权威字节不得由翻译覆盖；人类任务、说明和退出条件可以提供 译文或派生显示，并保留原文权威及证据身份。必须区分："
msgstr "Introduce bilingual terms where useful, then use one term per concept. C symbols, configuration keys, error codes, fields and machine identity values in CSV/JSON stay unchanged, including states, IDs, digests, paths, versions and configuration values. Translation must not overwrite authoritative CSV/JSON bytes. Human-facing tasks, explanations and exit conditions may have translations or derived displays while preserving original authority and evidence identities. Distinguish:"

msgid "术语"
msgstr "Term"

msgid "本文档体系中的含义"
msgstr "Meaning in these docs"

msgid "factory"
msgstr "factory"

msgid "返回该装配已有静态接口的typed查找"
msgstr "Typed lookup returning existing static interfaces of this assembly."

msgid "face"
msgstr "face"

msgid "公共只读接口，含ops和实例context"
msgstr "Public read-only interface containing ops and instance context."

msgid "provider"
msgstr "provider"

msgid "具体实现及私有状态"
msgstr "Concrete implementation and private state."

msgid "controller/endpoint"
msgstr "controller/endpoint"

msgid "控制器身份与其逻辑/外部端点身份"
msgstr "Controller identity versus logical/external endpoint identity."

msgid "owner/executor"
msgstr "owner/executor"

msgid "资源/生命周期责任与实际执行推进责任"
msgstr "Resource/lifecycle responsibility versus actual execution/progression responsibility."

msgid "request/buffer"
msgstr "request/buffer"

msgid "请求元数据与被借用的数据存储"
msgstr "Request metadata versus borrowed data storage."

msgid "DMA complete"
msgstr "DMA complete"

msgid "DMA阶段完成，尚需外设和引用排空"
msgstr "DMA phase complete; peripheral/reference drain remains."

msgid "wire complete"
msgstr "wire complete"

msgid "外设线上传输完成，尚需满足其余结束条件"
msgstr "Peripheral wire transfer complete; other final conditions remain."

msgid "SETTLED"
msgstr "SETTLED"

msgid "provider先排空必要引用，再以release发布SETTLED作为最后一次请求访问；调用方acquire观察"
msgstr "The provider drains required references, then release-publishes SETTLED as its final request access; the caller observes with acquire semantics."

msgid "QUARANTINED"
msgstr "QUARANTINED"

msgid "未安全结束，借用和恢复责任仍保留"
msgstr "Not safely ended; borrowing/recovery responsibility remains."

msgid "所有容量和测量写单位：B/KiB、Hz/MHz、cycles、µs/ms。Flash LOAD、Flash footprint、预留RAM和实测栈高水位分别记录。对齐、长度粒度、inclusive limit、 溢出、deadline时间域和最大配置须明确。理论上界、估计和实测值不能混写。"
msgstr "State capacity/measurement units: B/KiB, Hz/MHz, cycles and µs/ms. Record Flash LOAD, Flash footprint, reserved RAM and measured stack high-water separately. Define alignment, length granularity, inclusive limits, overflow, deadline domains and maximum configurations. Do not mix theoretical bounds, estimates and measurements."

msgid "有效约束示例：ACCEPTED后，调用方必须保持请求和缓冲区有效，直到acquire观察 SETTLED；复用相关adapter/observer存储还需对应引用排空。无效表述示例： “注意生命周期”。后者缺少主体、结束条件和失败责任。"
msgstr "Valid rule: after ACCEPTED, callers retain requests/buffers until acquire-observed SETTLED; reuse of adapter/observer storage also requires drained references. Invalid wording: “mind the lifecycle”, which omits actors, final conditions and failure responsibility."

msgid "3. 事实、计划和资格必须分别表达"
msgstr "3. Separate facts, plans and qualification"

msgid "表述"
msgstr "Claim"

msgid "必需依据"
msgstr "Required basis"

msgid "当前实现"
msgstr "Current implementation"

msgid "对应源码、配置/模式和行为范围"
msgstr "Corresponding source, configuration/mode and behavior scope."

msgid "已通过模型/Native"
msgstr "Model/Native pass"

msgid "精确源码、测试scope、实际执行结果"
msgstr "Exact source, test scope and actual execution."

msgid "ARM链接/资源验证"
msgstr "ARM link/resource validation"

msgid "对应配置、工具、ELF/BIN/map与检查"
msgstr "Configuration, tools, ELF/BIN/maps and checks."

msgid "软件候选"
msgstr "Software candidate"

msgid "clean source、SDK、实际复现和同产物证据"
msgstr "Clean source, SDK, actual reproducibility and same-artifact evidence."

msgid "实板通过"
msgstr "Physical pass"

msgid "PCB/芯片/设备/station/image和实际测量"
msgstr "PCB/chip/equipment/station/image and actual measurements."

msgid "计划或目标"
msgstr "Plan/target"

msgid "未实施任务及退出条件，不写成现有能力"
msgstr "Unimplemented tasks/exit conditions, never described as existing capabilities."

msgid "芯片具备、SDK提供、provider维护、Board授权、软件通过、HIL通过不能合并成 一个“支持”。当前、目标和参考配置必须在页面及图的caption中可见。文档发布 不建立新的平台资格。旧结果保留原始源码、失败尝试和状态，不能重标为新HEAD。"
msgstr "Chip features, SDK offerings, maintained providers, Board authorization, software passes and HIL passes cannot collapse into one “supported” label. Current/target/reference scope must be visible in pages and captions. Docs establish no new platform qualification. Retain original source, failed attempts and status; never relabel old results as current HEAD."

msgid "4. 示例与命令"
msgstr "4. Examples and commands"

msgid "完整例子必须来自维护fixture或固定版本外部示例，并关联实际consumer验证。 优先literalinclude；省略部分注明fragment原因。不能把示意片段称为完整教程。 普通构建不自动刷写、不执行任意Markdown命令，也不取得远程latest。"
msgstr "Complete examples must come from maintained fixtures or pinned external examples and be associated with actual consumer validation. Prefer literalinclude and explain fragments. Illustrations are not complete tutorials. Ordinary builds do not automatically flash devices, execute arbitrary Markdown commands or fetch remote latest."

msgid "每个命令说明工作目录、工具和连接前提、输入、预期结果、检查成功方法、清理。 固件C示例遵守现有C11、80列、四空格、附着大括号、类型侧指针和反斜杠 Doxygen风格。工具及测试示例遵守对应语言规范，包括现有Python工具和C++17 GoogleTest/GoogleMock用法。文档规则不重新定义仓库代码风格。"
msgstr "Every command states working directory, tools/connections, inputs, expected results, success checks and cleanup. Firmware C examples retain C11, 80 columns, four spaces, attached braces, type-side pointers and backslash Doxygen. Tool/test examples retain language conventions, including Python and C++17 GoogleTest/GoogleMock. Docs do not redefine code style."

msgid "异步例子必须说明拒绝、接受借用、执行推进、等待、取消、排空及结束后资源。 timeout/cancel不自动撤销借用；失败停止保留QUARANTINED存储。唤醒只是提示， 不能用无限等待掩盖推进条件。产品任务、私有分区和恢复政策仍属于外部工程。"
msgstr "Async examples must explain rejection, accepted borrowing, progression, waits, cancel, drain and final resources. Timeout/cancel does not revoke borrows; failed stops retain QUARANTINED storage. Wakeups are hints, and infinite waits cannot conceal progression conditions. Tasks, private partitions and recovery stay external."

msgid "5. 图示身份与关系"
msgstr "5. Diagram identity and relationships"

msgid "每张图至少有ID、名称、用途、类型、适用范围、关系图例、正文合同和来源。 ID用于目录和迁移；公共anchor使用标准显式target/label，不能依靠front matter 自动产生引用。图源与输出登记在 {download}`图册清单 <../assets/diagrams/diagram-index.csv>`。"
msgstr "Every diagram must have at least an ID, name, purpose, type, scope, relation legend, prose contract and source. IDs support indexes/migration; public anchors use explicit targets/labels rather than automatic front-matter references. Register pairs in the {download}`diagram index <../assets/diagrams/diagram-index.csv>`."

msgid "图的身份"
msgstr "Diagram identity"

msgid "允许表达"
msgstr "Allowed meaning"

msgid "不得暗示"
msgstr "Must not imply"

msgid "current"
msgstr "current"

msgid "经源码核对的结构/契约"
msgstr "Source-checked structure/contracts."

msgid "整个平台、所有模式或实板均通过"
msgstr "All platforms/modes or physical Boards passed."

msgid "target"
msgstr "target"

msgid "已制定但待实施的设计"
msgstr "Defined design awaiting implementation."

msgid "新模块/工具已存在或已部署"
msgstr "New modules/tools already exist or are deployed."

msgid "reference"
msgstr "reference"

msgid "精确芯片/板卡/模式的参考装配"
msgstr "Exact chip/Board/mode reference assembly."

msgid "自动推广到其他平台、PCB和安全域"
msgstr "Automatic applicability to other platforms, PCBs or security domains."

msgid "一张图解决一个主要问题。分层图、编译依赖图、生成流程、数据流、时序和状态图 分别表达对应关系；混合关系时逐边标明含义。跨边界箭头必须可解释，不能同时 把未标记箭头理解为调用、生成和所有权转移。"
msgstr "One diagram answers one primary question. Layering, build dependencies, generation, data, sequences and states have distinct relations; label each edge when mixed. Explain cross-boundary arrows; unlabeled arrows cannot simultaneously mean calls, generation and ownership transfers."

msgid "节点名对应源码、接口或明确概念；可选项必须有文字或线型标记，不能只靠颜色。 返回箭头、异步事件、状态迁移的方向准确。图不会因美化增加不存在的CPU factory、 隐藏任务、统一池或强制OS层。"
msgstr "Nodes name source, interfaces or explicit concepts. Mark optional elements with text/line styles, not color alone. Returns, asynchronous events and state transitions point correctly. Aesthetic changes must not invent CPU factories, hidden tasks, unified pools or mandatory OS layers."

msgid "6. 必需图册与语义检查"
msgstr "6. Required diagram set and semantic checks"

msgid "下列图分别对应DOC-43至DOC-57，具体顺序与退出条件在实施台账。"
msgstr "The following diagrams correspond to DOC-43–DOC-57; order/exit conditions are in the ledger."

msgid "图ID"
msgstr "Diagram ID"

msgid "内容"
msgstr "Content"

msgid "必须表达的关键事实"
msgstr "Required key facts"

msgid "FIG-01"
msgstr "FIG-01"

msgid "全平台架构与外部边界"
msgstr "Whole-platform architecture and external boundaries"

msgid "产品外置，Core/Arch/SoC/I/O，组件和OS可选"
msgstr "External products; Core/Arch/SoC/I/O; optional components/OS."

msgid "FIG-02"
msgstr "FIG-02"

msgid "编译目标依赖"
msgstr "Build-target dependencies"

msgid "从实际CMake核对，SDK私有，应用依赖平台"
msgstr "Checked against actual CMake; private SDK; applications depend on platform."

msgid "FIG-03"
msgstr "FIG-03"

msgid "配置和生成"
msgstr "Configuration/generation"

msgid "TOML+facts→typed IR→原子bundle→CMake→产物；失败失效"
msgstr "TOML+facts→typed IR→atomic bundle→CMake→artifacts; failures invalidate."

msgid "FIG-04"
msgstr "FIG-04"

msgid "factory/实例结构"
msgstr "Factory/instance structure"

msgid "既有face、共享ops、独立context；controller与endpoint"
msgstr "Existing faces, shared ops, separate contexts; controller/endpoint identities."

msgid "FIG-05"
msgstr "FIG-05"

msgid "初始化与失败撤回"
msgstr "Initialization/failed-start withdrawal"

msgid "显式启动、部分效果、逆序撤回、失败保留责任"
msgstr "Explicit startup, partial effects, reverse withdrawal and retained failure responsibility."

msgid "FIG-06"
msgstr "FIG-06"

msgid "请求状态"
msgstr "Request states"

msgid "拒绝/借用/排空/隔离/SETTLED，观察者另需退出"
msgstr "Rejection/borrowing/draining/quarantine/SETTLED; observers exit separately."

msgid "FIG-07"
msgstr "FIG-07"

msgid "UART/SPI DMA时序"
msgstr "UART/SPI DMA sequences"

msgid "DMA TC、线上完成、引用排空与最终发布分开"
msgstr "Separate DMA TC, wire completion, reference drain and final publication."

msgid "FIG-08"
msgstr "FIG-08"

msgid "wait/wake/退出"
msgstr "Wait/wake/shutdown"

msgid "ready-arm-ready-wait-ready，执行器和join责任"
msgstr "ready-arm-ready-wait-ready, executor and join responsibility."

msgid "FIG-09"
msgstr "FIG-09"

msgid "CPU/内存/DMA/Cache"
msgstr "CPU/memory/DMA/Cache"

msgid "精确配置、可达域、完整cache line与维护时点"
msgstr "Exact configurations, reachable domains, whole cache lines and maintenance timing."

msgid "FIG-10"
msgstr "FIG-10"

msgid "SDK消费"
msgstr "SDK consumption"

msgid "实际外部工程、搬移、配置/链接/运行和产物检查"
msgstr "Actual external projects, relocation, configure/link/run and artifact checks."

msgid "FIG-11"
msgstr "FIG-11"

msgid "软件与HIL证据"
msgstr "Software/HIL evidence"

msgid "各自实际取得，再按scope准入；不自动生成物理资格"
msgstr "Acquired independently then admitted by scope; no automatic physical qualification."

msgid "FIG-12"
msgstr "FIG-12"

msgid "文档/SDK发布与恢复"
msgstr "Docs/SDK publication and recovery"

msgid "身份、不可变版本、离线包、下载和独立恢复"
msgstr "Identities, immutable versions, offline packages, downloads and independent restoration."

msgid "FIG-13"
msgstr "FIG-13"

msgid "Cortex-M能力分层"
msgstr "Cortex-M capability layers"

msgid "原语、Runtime、SoC接入、实板资格分别表达"
msgstr "Primitives, Runtime, SoC integration and physical qualification are separate."

msgid "FIG-14"
msgstr "FIG-14"

msgid "U575双域"
msgstr "U575 dual worlds"

msgid "仅选定TZEN=1同步参考；SAU/MPU/GTZC/gateway责任"
msgstr "Selected TZEN=1 synchronous reference only; SAU/MPU/GTZC/gateway responsibilities."

msgid "FIG-15"
msgstr "FIG-15"

msgid "连续流与丢块"
msgstr "Continuous streams and lost blocks"

msgid "producer/block/consumer、overrun和停止排空；服务预算"
msgstr "producer/block/consumer, overrun, stop/drain and service budgets."

msgid "运行图必须让读者看到：factory取得已有接口以后，日常I/O直接通过face进入 provider；Arch按编译目标选择；应用拥有调度和执行进度。初始化顺序不能由静态 结构图推断，静态结构图也不能代表运行时每次调用路径。"
msgstr "Runtime diagrams must show that after factory lookup, ordinary I/O calls faces/providers directly; Arch is compile-target-selected; applications own scheduling/progression. Static structure does not determine initialization order or represent every runtime call."

msgid "状态图中REJECTED/ACCEPTED是admission结果，不伪造为nx_request_state_t状态。 SETTLED只在全部必要引用排空后发布；取消/deadline不能直接指向“存储已释放”。 QUARANTINED到结束必须有实际恢复/排空证明，不暗示每个provider都有恢复API。 时序图必须包含相关失败分支或链接独立失败图，并标清Task/IRQ/DMA/安全域。"
msgstr "REJECTED/ACCEPTED are admission outcomes, not invented nx_request_state_t enum states. Publish SETTLED only after required reference drain; cancel/deadlines never point directly to reclaimed storage. Ending QUARANTINED needs actual recovery/drain proof without implying every provider has recovery APIs. Sequence diagrams must include failure branches or link separate failure diagrams, with Task/IRQ/DMA/security domains marked."

msgid "图不能替代正文的调用前提与权威合同。图文冲突时暂停相关交付结论并修正来源， 不能只改图或教程隐藏规范冲突。"
msgstr "Diagrams do not replace preconditions/contracts. Conflicts suspend affected delivery claims until sources are corrected; changing diagrams/tutorials alone must not hide contract conflicts."

msgid "7. 图源、视觉和离线交付"
msgstr "7. Sources, visual quality and offline delivery"

msgid "首批采用可编辑Graphviz DOT和本地SVG，图源与输出成对保存。Sphinx后续可用 内置graphviz扩展；新图链及工具锁仍按DOC-25/33实施。既有Mermaid作为迁移输入， 不能另维护同一图的第二份权威源。需要时序专用工具时，以实际需求另行审查闭包。"
msgstr "Initially use editable Graphviz DOT and local SVG pairs. Sphinx may later use its graphviz extension; new chains/locks follow DOC-25/33. Existing Mermaid is migration input, not another authority for the same diagram. Specialized sequence tools need independently reviewed closures justified by real demand."

msgid "每张图同时满足："
msgstr "Every diagram satisfies:"

msgid "图源可审查，图名/ID稳定；图源变更后重新生成输出。"
msgstr "Reviewable source and stable names/IDs; regenerate after source changes."

msgid "深色文字与清楚边界；颜色不是唯一含义，灰度下仍可区分。"
msgstr "Dark text/clear boundaries; colors are not sole meaning and grayscale remains distinguishable."

msgid "标签短且具体，复杂说明放正文；过密时拆图，不缩小到无法阅读。"
msgstr "Short specific labels with detailed prose; split dense diagrams rather than shrinking unreadably."

msgid "中文、英文、C符号完整，无缺字、重叠、裁切和模糊截图。"
msgstr "Complete Chinese/English/C symbols without missing glyphs, overlap, clipping or blurry screenshots."

msgid "提供alt和caption；窄屏可以放大或独立打开SVG，不把整图强制缩成小字。"
msgstr "Alt text/captions; narrow screens allow zoom/standalone SVG rather than forcing tiny text."

msgid "SVG默认无脚本、动画、foreignObject、外部href/资源及DOCTYPE。"
msgstr "SVG defaults exclude scripts, animation, foreignObject, external href/resources and DOCTYPE."

msgid "图和图源随离线包交付，加载、字体说明与检查不依赖CDN。"
msgstr "Offline packages include diagrams/sources; loading, font notes and checks need no CDN."

msgid "Graphviz及实际字体进入文档工具闭包，缺失或差异不伪称已验证。"
msgstr "Graphviz/actual fonts belong to tool closure; missing/different tools never claim validation."

msgid "SVG解析和渲染成功不证明架构正确。独立审查必须逐边核对调用/依赖、状态和 失败责任。实际显示需要检查桌面、窄屏/放大和打印；未执行项保留未验证状态。"
msgstr "Successful SVG parsing/rendering does not prove architecture correctness. Independent review must check every call/dependency, state and failure edge. Actual display checks desktop, narrow/zoom and print; unexecuted checks remain unverified."

msgid "8. 评审与自动化职责"
msgstr "8. Review and automation responsibilities"

msgid "检查"
msgstr "Check"

msgid "机器可负责"
msgstr "Machine responsibility"

msgid "独立语义审查负责"
msgstr "Independent semantic responsibility"

msgid "正文"
msgstr "Prose"

msgid "格式、字段、链接、anchor、导航"
msgstr "Formatting, fields, links, anchors and navigation."

msgid "任务完整、前提准确、术语清楚"
msgstr "Complete tasks, correct prerequisites and clear terminology."

msgid "示例"
msgstr "Examples"

msgid "实际解析/构建、固定输入与退出码"
msgstr "Actual parsing/building, pinned inputs and exits."

msgid "正常/失败/恢复和所有权正确"
msgstr "Correct success/failure/recovery and ownership."

msgid "图"
msgstr "Diagrams"

msgid "图源语法、文件配对、SVG资源、哈希"
msgstr "Source syntax, pairs, SVG resources and hashes."

msgid "箭头/可选项/时序/状态与代码一致"
msgstr "Arrows/options/sequences/states match code."

msgid "翻译"
msgstr "Translation"

msgid "源版本、缺译/fuzzy、状态"
msgstr "Source versions, missing/fuzzy messages and status."

msgid "规范强度、单位和失败条件保持"
msgstr "Preserved normative strength, units and failure conditions."

msgid "交付"
msgstr "Delivery"

msgid "manifest、相对链接、实际站点身份"
msgstr "Manifests, relative links and actual site identity."

msgid "支持/计划/资格边界没有混淆"
msgstr "No confusion of support, plans or qualification."

msgid "不通过正则扫描正文来自动判定“支持”或“安全”。新增gate行为采用实际负路径 TDD；纯正文和图源修改采用对应检查与语义评审，不新增镜像实现测试。"
msgstr "Regex prose scanning never automatically decides “supported” or “safe”. New gate behavior uses actual negative-path TDD. Prose/diagram-source changes use applicable checks/semantic review without implementation-mirroring tests."

msgid "审查记录至少绑定页面/图、代码与文档来源、发现、处理结果和退出条件。下列情况 必须修正后才能关闭相应任务：错误配置、借用提前回收、错误完成顺序、图中虚构 模块、错误支持/HIL声明、断链、未标注的过期翻译、关键图无法阅读。"
msgstr "Reviews bind pages/diagrams, code/docs sources, findings, resolution and exit conditions. Correct these before closing tasks: invalid configurations, early borrow reclamation, wrong completion order, invented modules, false support/HIL, broken links, unmarked stale translations or unreadable critical diagrams."

msgid "完整标准应用和58项系统实施以台账实际状态为准。快速提交检查、严格文档CI、 图源/输出配对和全部当前页面的中英文翻译检查由统一CLI执行。原文摘要、审查 标记和严格构建新提取的完整消息集合同时有效；缺译、过期或 fuzzy 必须修复。 混合语言原文可采用同源语言 catalog，代码、标识符和原证据值保持原样。 历史归档不参与当前翻译完成判定；独立语义、视觉、发布与恢复结果 分别绑定实际输入，不从规则或工作流存在推断执行完成。"
msgstr "Ledger state determines standard application and 58-item implementation acceptance. Unified CLI runs offline commit checks, strict CI, source/output pairing and English/Chinese checks for every current page. Source digests, review markers and newly extracted complete strict-build message sets must all agree; missing/stale/fuzzy translations fail. Mixed sources may use source-language catalogs while code, identifiers and original evidence remain unchanged. Archives do not count toward current translation completion. Semantic, visual, publication and restoration records bind actual inputs; rules/workflows alone never establish execution."

msgid "9. 源码相邻 README"
msgstr "9. Source-adjacent READMEs"

msgid "平台自有的当前 README 以中文维护，保留代码符号、配置键、命令、单位和证据身份。 根 `README.md` 是中文总入口，`README_CN.md` 仅保留旧链接导航。中英文站点继续使用 同源正文和已审 gettext；不在同一 README 后追加一份可能漂移的另一语言合同。 第三方原文、许可证、绑定来源身份的导入说明和冻结证据保留原字节；需要中文说明时， 由当前外层导航解释其范围并链接原件。"
msgstr "Maintain current platform-owned READMEs in Chinese while preserving code symbols, configuration keys, commands, units and evidence identities. Root `README.md` is the Chinese entry point; `README_CN.md` retains only navigation for old links. English/Chinese sites continue to use one canonical source and reviewed gettext. Do not append a second-language contract that can drift within the same README. Preserve third-party originals, licenses, source-identity-bound import notes and frozen evidence byte for byte. When Chinese explanation is needed, current outer navigation explains scope and links the original."

msgid "README 是从目录进入架构的入口。一级层解释职责、上下游、目录和代码入口、状态／ 资源所有者、主要调用链、成本与限制；SoC 解释精确型号和模式；Board 解释已审连接、 电气、硬件选择和未知事实；组件解释窄端口、存储、执行者和完整停止。工具／测试入口 解释实际输入输出、命令、失败和验证边界。仅在存在明确维护价值的目录增加入口， 不为每一级文件夹机械建页，不抄公共头形成另一份 API 签名合同。"
msgstr "READMEs provide an entry into architecture from a directory. Top-level layers explain responsibilities, upstream/downstream relationships, directory/code entry points, state/resource ownership, main call chains, costs and limitations. SoC pages explain exact parts and modes. Board pages explain reviewed connections, electrical conditions, hardware selections and unknown facts. Component pages explain narrow ports, storage, executors and complete stop. Tool/test entry points explain actual inputs/outputs, commands, failures and verification boundaries. Add an entry point only where it has clear maintenance value; do not mechanically create a page for every directory level or copy public headers into a second API-signature contract."

msgid "已有中英文追加段落须按主题合并并核对双方独有约束；迁移独有正文必须更新引用并 保留唯一权威。不得用删行数或固定字数取代语义完整性。长页提供主题导航；历史结果 明确绑定原 source／scope，不能写成当前资格。架构变化核对已有图册，引用 SVG 和图源， 不要另画一套同义图。"
msgstr "Merge existing appended English/Chinese passages by topic and check constraints unique to either language. Moving unique content requires updated references and one canonical authority. Do not substitute line-count reductions or fixed word limits for semantic completeness. Provide topic navigation on long pages. Bind historical results explicitly to their original source/scope rather than presenting current qualification. Check architecture changes against the existing figure atlas and reference its SVGs/sources instead of drawing a second equivalent figure."

msgid "被站点 include 的 README 改动须重新实际 gettext 提取，更新父页面语言、摘要和完整 消息集合；普通非站点 README 另按修改清单检查本地链接、锚点和命令。SDK 携带的 README 核对真实 payload 中的目标；引用仓库独有 docs／tests 时，声明完整 checkout 上下文及按 manifest 的 source commit 阅读原仓库的方法，不声称 SDK 内全部相对链接 可离线使用。文档改写不修改旧 SDK／归档摘要。独立评审检查 规范强度、所有权、失败责任、精确模式和支持边界，工具检查不能替代该评审。"
msgstr "Changes to site-included READMEs require fresh actual gettext extraction and updates to the parent page’s language, digest and complete message set. Separately check local links, anchors and commands in ordinary non-site READMEs against the change inventory. Verify targets against the actual payload for SDK-carried READMEs. When referring to repository-only docs/tests, state the full-checkout context and how to read the original repository at the manifest’s source commit; do not claim all SDK-relative links work offline. Documentation edits must not modify old SDK/archive digests. Independent review checks normative strength, ownership, failure responsibilities, exact modes and support boundaries; tool checks cannot replace that review."
